# V13.14.4 Connection + Auto Market Polish

Focused patch from the provided clean ZIP. No broad UI rebuild.

## Fixed
- Frontend REST calls now default to a same-origin Next proxy at `/api/backend`. This prevents the deployed frontend from falling back to `127.0.0.1:8000` in the visitor browser.
- Added `frontend/app/api/backend/[...path]/route.ts` proxy. Railway frontend service must set `BACKEND_URL` to the backend service URL.
- Backend CORS regex fixed for Railway and local dev. Bare `CORS_ORIGINS=*` no longer breaks CORS normalization.
- Auto Market live ticks now include `live_market` status, so 2x/5x do not snap back to 1x after the next WebSocket tick.
- Frontend only updates Auto Market state when a real `enabled` field exists. Empty live payloads no longer reset the toggle.
- Button state remains `Auto Market` / `Pause Market` based on backend status.
- 1x remains the normal baseline; 2x and 5x only shorten tick intervals.
- Candle time index is now monotonic and does not repeat after history trimming. This targets the long-session chart collapse / one-candle bug.

## Railway frontend variables
Set these on the **frontend service**:

```env
BACKEND_URL=[link removed]
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=wss://YOUR-BACKEND.up.railway.app
```

`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` can stay empty when using the proxy. If you set it, it should be the real backend URL, never `127.0.0.1`.

## Backend variables
Usually no custom CORS variable is needed. If you set one manually, use:

```env
CORS_ORIGIN_REGEX=[link removed]
```


